# Patch 0077 — Blocked-today badge on the ⚙ menu (ROADMAP Phase 4 follow-up;
# the last open Phase 4 item). The Privacy Center pane had today's blocked-
# tracker count but nowhere on a chrome surface showed it.
#
# WHAT: a third pinned row in the Kavacha ⚙ menu (beside Settings and
# Appearance) reading "N trackers blocked today", which opens the Privacy
# Center (paneKavachaPrivacy) on click. The count comes from the SAME source
# the pane reads — PrivacyMetricsService.getTodayStats() over
# protections.sqlite — so the badge and the pane never disagree.
#
# WHY the menu, not the toolbar: a pinned menu row matches the existing
# Settings/Appearance destinations, needs no customizable-widget plumbing, and
# leaves the horizontal URL row (patch 0010) untouched. It reads as one place
# with the pane it opens (shares the tracking-protection icon).
#
# DETAILS: the count is async, so the row ships a static "Trackers blocked
# today" label and fills in the number when the ledger resolves; a
# `.isConnected` guard drops a late resolve after the panel closed, and the
# panel rebuilds on every open so the figure is always today's. Private
# windows have no ledger and get no row. The pinned-search entry is updated to
# the counted label so the filter still finds it.
#
# Marionette-verified on the built browser: with 7 events seeded for today, the
# menu's pinned rows are [Settings, Appearance, "7 trackers blocked today"] and
# the badge's command opens paneKavachaPrivacy.
diff --git a/locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-command-palette.ftl b/locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-command-palette.ftl
index 4a52cd8..175be8d 100644
--- a/locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-command-palette.ftl
+++ b/locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-command-palette.ftl
@@ -74,6 +74,15 @@ kavacha-menu-no-results = Nothing matches that
 # Kavacha patch 0063 — the Appearance panel. Replaces the menu's generated
 # Appearance section with one place that shows the colours.
 kavacha-menu-appearance = Appearance
+
+# Kavacha patch 0077 — blocked-today badge. The static label shows before the
+# ledger resolves; the count label replaces it with today's number.
+kavacha-menu-blocked-loading = Trackers blocked today
+kavacha-menu-blocked-today =
+    { $count ->
+        [one] { $count } tracker blocked today
+       *[other] { $count } trackers blocked today
+    }
 kavacha-appearance-title = Appearance
 kavacha-appearance-mode-dark = Dark
 kavacha-appearance-mode-light = Light
